(# Information retrieval: precision and recall) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Information retrieval is the task of finding material in an unstructured store that) Tj T*
(matches an information need.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Precision measures the fraction of retrieved documents that are relevant. Recall) Tj T*
(measures the fraction of relevant documents that were retrieved. The two pull in) Tj T*
(opposite directions: returning more documents raises recall and lowers precision.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A ranked retrieval system returns an ordered list, so a cutoff at rank k gives a) Tj T*
(precision-at-k figure. The break-even point is where precision equals recall.) Tj T*
ET
